cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research reference implementation, please cite this software version and the related paper listed in CITATION.md."
type: software
title: "Delegation grant reference-monitor companion"
version: 1.0.2
authors:
  - family-names: Fassio
    given-names: Ed
    affiliation: ByteBrain LLC
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Deterministic, single-process research reference implementation of a proposed
  decision-scoped delegation grant, with a machine-readable schema, predeclared
  synthetic fixtures, a shared-budget differential, and explicit trust and
  implementation limits. Accompanies Decision-Scoped Delegation for AI Systems,
  public-facing edition 1.1 (2026).
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - decision-scoped delegation
  - human sponsorship
  - reference monitor
  - synthetic evaluation
references:
  - type: book
    title: "The Constitution of the Frontier: What Must Remain True, No Matter How Intelligent the Machines Become"
    authors:
      - family-names: Fassio
        given-names: Ed
    year: 2026
    edition: "First"
    url: "https://edfassio.com/books/the-constitution-of-the-frontier/"
